    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d384">

                <pb facs="0912" n="878" xml:id="pg878"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">396.1 BE/1–2954 Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 384<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of
                            State to the Department of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >niact</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-01-29T18:00:00+01:00">January 29, 1954—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Dulte 17. Eyes only for Acting Secretary. We
                    start immediately preparing position and tactics with British and French for
                    restricted meeting of four Ministers next week. I intend to submit tomorrow to
                    working group now set up by three Western delegations substance of proposal
                    contained in Dulte 10<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d384-f1"/> and approved by Tedul
                        5.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d384-f2"/> I would hope this could then become basis
                    for agreed position of Bidault, Eden and myself.</p>
                <p>I would appreciate, therefore, any necessary preparations in Washington being
                    started at once, including, I would think, notifying confidentially USUN, Arthur Dean<anchor
                        n="3" xml:id="d384-f3"/> and American Embassy Seoul in view possibility
                    leaks from British or French. Of course we cannot be sure British–French
                    concurrence so project must be regarded highly tentative.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
